# Changelog

All notable changes to this project are documented in this file.

## [Unreleased]

### Added

- Watering history API: `activity` and `activity_type` DynamoDB tables (with a `plant_id`/`activity_date` GSI for per-plant history lookups), backing `ActivityRepository`/`ActivityTypeRepository`, `ActivityService`/`ActivityTypeService`, and REST handlers — `POST/GET /plants/{id}/activities`, `DELETE /plants/{id}/activities/{activityId}`, `GET /activity-types`
- Watering history widget on plant detail: a Mon–Sun heatmap spanning 6 months with a "last watered" summary, now backed by real logged activity data
- Water button on plant detail logs a real watering activity via the API and refreshes the history
- Icon action row (Photo/Water/Edit/Delete) replacing the old upload button/edit-delete row
- Icons on care preference and info fields (location, acquired, humidity, temperature, light, watering, check daily, fertilize)

### Changed

- Plant detail page layout: independent left/right columns so card heights no longer stretch to match a taller sibling; watering history card now sits directly after the plant info card, both on desktop and mobile
- Card borders on plant detail and plant list switched from the low-contrast hairline token to the stronger border token so cards read clearly against the page background
- Plant list cards enlarged on mobile (bigger thumbnail, padding, and title size) for easier tapping
- Mobile card spacing aligned to the same 16px rhythm used on desktop
- Terraform documentation added; API request handling improved (better error handling, requirements/providers/resources docs)
- Lambda IAM policy extended with `dynamodb:Query` and access to the new `activity`/`activity_type` tables and GSI
- API Gateway CORS allowlist extended to include local dev origins

### Fixed

- Form input styling: set min-width to 0 for better layout consistency
- Delete button hover no longer spills a pill-shaped background past the circular icon
- API responses containing DynamoDB numeric fields (e.g. `activity_type_id`) no longer 500 — `json_response` now serializes `Decimal` values correctly

## [0.3.0] - 2026-08-16 — Infrastructure & hardening

### Added

- Terraform infrastructure for AWS: S3, DynamoDB, API Gateway, IAM roles, Lambda, and Amplify
- Plant management API: full CRUD operations and image upload handling
- Date-acquired input on plant detail/form
- Icons on plant detail action buttons

### Changed

- Plant editing functionality; S3 client configuration; API Gateway CORS settings
- Plant form: radio-button pill selection for status and humidity
- Plant detail and list UI: button styles, card layout, filter count display
- Photo upload section on plant detail page
- Form input styles: line height, box-sizing, custom select dropdown appearance
- Image upload: added content type handling and upload confirmation step
- `PlantRepository` attribute names updated to match DynamoDB schema
- API base URL updated for the development environment

### Fixed

- Error handling: `PlantRepository` now raises exceptions properly; clearer API client error responses

## [0.2.0] - 2026-08-15 — Backend & modularization

### Added

- Plant management features: forms, rendering, and API integration
- Status filters on plant list/detail pages
- Tech stack details added to README

### Changed

- Reorganized JavaScript into modular per-page scripts; updated HTML references for maintainability
- Plant detail rendering and styling: scientific name handling, card layout, CSS polish
- Plant detail and list pages: HTML structure and CSS improvements
- Navigation updated across plant management pages

## [0.1.0] - 2026-07-24 to 2026-08-13 — Initial UI (HTML/CSS/JS)

### Added

- Initial project scaffold with plain HTML/CSS/JS front end
- Plant form for adding/editing plants
- Plant detail rendering with delete functionality
- Single-file `plant-backend.py` prototype and basic API client
- OpenAPI specification; README functional/non-functional requirements
- HTML-escaping utility for safer status message display
- Environment variable support for API base URL configuration

### Changed

- Project restructure
- API client refactored to support dynamic base URL and improved error handling

### Fixed

- Import statement for client module in plant API
- Plant form bugs
